        "The base interval is the strategy interval (5m): the data is supplied only at 5 minutes, the second row of the base-interval table.",
        "Quantities and prices are chosen so every average price and every target quantity is exact: no tick rounding (SPEC-03) and no fraction rounding (SPEC-13) is involved.",
        "Three scaling rules are not settled by the documents and decide most numbers here. SPEC-08: an add made before any target has filled gives every target its original fraction of the tranche (0.5 and 0.3) and the rest (0.2) to the remainder. SPEC-09: an add made after target 0 has filled gives the unfilled target its original fraction, 0.3, and the rest, including the filled target's 0.5, to the remainder. SPEC-10: unfilled target levels follow the average price, like the stop.",
        "Other readings, same bars. SPEC-08 alternative (the first add does not join the targets): target 0 sells 50. SPEC-09 alternative (the second add is split between the unfilled target and the remainder in their original relative proportions, 0.3 : 0.2): target 1 sells 120 and the trail takes 80, gross P&L 4400.00. SPEC-10 alternative (targets keep the levels set at the first fill): target 0 fills at 1010.00 and target 1 at 1020.00, each in the same slice as here.",
        "The entry bar 09:20 has high equal to open. The trail is armed by 09:35 under either reference (average price or first entry) and stays armed after the second add under either reading, so SPEC-01 and SPEC-12 do not matter. No add bar touches the old or the new stop or target, so SPEC-11 does not matter."
